WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:08.019 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  [Music]  one of the problems of living in new  zealand and attempting to create videos  for games that i enjoy is that most of  the major announcements and content  drops happen at some ungodly time in the  morning so i'm usually only seeing the  tail end of the hype throughout the  community unless i've been made aware  beforehand  today as of writing the script when i  woke up people were still buzzing about  a couple of announcements  one of them being the launch trailer  release for operation motherland  if you haven't seen it i'll have a link  in the description or you could always  look it up yourself  anyway i'd suggest you watch that first  if you'd like to make any sense of this  video  so i won't beat around the bush here  will this update from what we can see in  the trailer have an impact on the  quality of life and break point  i'll be the first to admit other than  jumping in to complete the smaller  events that have popped up i haven't  really put too many hours into the game  outside of the initial campaign  it just didn't maintain my attention for  an open world game although beautiful  and aesthetically pleasing it felt dead  i have no ambition to repeat missions  and outside of these there really isn't  all that much going on out there  especially when compared to wildlands  where there would be truckloads of  civilians mulling about doing their  thing with hostiles dotted throughout  well i feel like this update might be  addressing this  but before i get into that let's talk  about the story as you know this is what  initially drew me to these tom clancy  games  after the events of operation greenstone  where the ghost would go on to take down  walker and the bulk of his wolves nomad  and his team lee varroa having now  completed their mission  however months later the island quickly  became a strategic place for powerful  countries who are looking to get hold of  the technology contained within  seeing this threat the cia has tasked an  old friend of the ghosts karen bowman  with diffusing the potential of this  global crisis  the cia aims to ease global tensions by  giving power on the island to a neutral  force haruhi ito and the outcasts  turning a roar into an autonomous  country  but in order to do this they're going to  need some help so the ghosts have been  sent back to assist the outcasts with  removing the remaining hostile forces on  the island  sentinel and the wolves are still  wreaking havoc but there is another  enemy recently seen on the island that  has also joined the fight  the bodaks  and this time they have brought  helicopters vehicles and greater numbers  so there we have it i especially like  how they've avoided without saying the  events of the smaller operations that  have occurred since greenstone the story  of col d walker really was the best  narrative piece and i'm certainly not  upset that the other ops on aurora are  sort of being ignored at this point  however the biggest question i see being  asked from this trailer is when and how  did nomad and his team leave the island  and i get it they've been stuck there  fighting away with no support because of  the drone swarm stopping anyone from  entering and exiting the island  but i don't really see this as story  breaking  unlike other ludicrous editions i'm  looking at you terminator event there  have been so many situations where the  ghosts have been able to assist various  people with escaping opening up holes in  the drone defense to allow entry or exit  the biggest question i have is why did  the ghosts leave  there was obviously a large enough force  of sentinel and wolves still active  beyond what the outcasts could handle  maybe they were called away for  something more important elsewhere  forgetting that what they were leaving  behind was as powerful as it is  perhaps they thought the outcasts would  be fine but the introduction of the  bodaks tipped them over the edge  i don't know but like i keep saying to  people in the comments hopefully the  motherland update will answer these  questions for us we shall see  anyway for now let's get back to what i  was saying about the liveliness of  aurora  operation motherland is introducing a  new mode to the game called conquest  this is an alternative mode to the  breakpoint story mode where player  actions have consequences on what  happens throughout aurora  basically this is a territory control  type situation where we will be faced  with a number of objectives that we're  familiar with like destroying staff  securing camps stealing things from the  enemy and choosing to extract or  eliminate lieutenants who are dotted  around the map  the outcome of these events will lead to  changes on aurora  taking down enemies will show an  increase in outcast presence in the area  leading to an increase in faction  warfare in the territory  each territory will have different  challenges but based on the strength of  the faction power there will be a change  in checkpoints convoys hostage  situations and patrols  this all sounds eerily similar to what  we have in the division too with control  points and factions taking over  different districts  but at this stage it appears to be a  little more dynamic than the open world  activity in the division  however this is a whole new game mode  anyone familiar with the division will  know how repetitive this can be  capturing everything just for it to flip  back over after a set period of time  i'm hoping motherland will be a bit  different offering more replayability  rather than something that just ends up  feeling like more of a chore after the  first couple of times of doing it  but in saying that it'll still add a  hell of a lot more life to an  environment that has been lacking it  since the beginning  i'm just looking forward to having a  reason to explore the whole map again  again talking to the liveliness of  aurora a larger variety of atmospheric  conditions will be added  with the region being split into five  different zones the weather condition  will also change depending on where you  are including the cloudiness rain fog  conditions and sunniness  but also the environmental effects  including insects fumes grasses and bird  flight have been adjusted  and no this doesn't mean a static  weather system the conditions will vary  day by day for each zone  i like this it's the little things that  make a big difference to me  obviously we'll also be seeing a large  range of bug fixes throughout the game  as well as a number of well overdue  quality of life improvements  i'll have a link to this list in the  description  last but certainly not least the bodaks  i'm actually disappointed with myself  that i haven't made a video on these  guys they're certainly one of the more  interesting factions of the ghost recon  universe  maybe i'll get onto that soon  like i said earlier they're back on  aurora  allied to sentinel and the wolves  they'll be the largest challenge going  forward  they'll be arriving on narosh shores  sporting five different archetypes  troopers the standard bodak soldier  tacticians who will call for backup  oppressors heavily armoured rushes  dreadnoughts armed with rocket launchers  and seekers who will use rifles and  optical camouflage  also with the introduction of the bodak  we'll be seeing a large influx of new  russian weapons and vehicle skins as  well as a number of new items in maria's  shop  motherland appears to be breakpoint's  biggest update yet  do i think it will be game changing  it certainly looks promising i'm  cautiously optimistic  i'll hold my final judgment until i've  actually been able to sit down and play  through it properly but i'm excited at  the potential  at the very least i think this is a very  good start and i hope that they continue  to build on the game with initiatives  like this  in the meantime i'm super rusty so i  think i'll jump in and dust off the  characters in preparation for the  release  thanks for watching and i'll catch in  the next one cheers  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]

